  "hints": [
    "Only the preceding row is needed, so a single array can be reused.",
    "Update interior values from right to left to retain both old parents until they are used.",
    "Append one for the new boundary, then add row[j-1] into row[j] for descending interior indices.",
    "Row index zero needs no updates."
  ],
  "editorial": "Start with [1]. Each iteration extends the array with a final one and updates the interior in descending index order. This order preserves each previous-row value until its last use, unlike a left-to-right update. The final array has row_index+1 entries and uses linear extra space; the reference recurrence takes quadratic time.",
